 "what": "Whether this decoder's object output is right on the 89 library titles Dolby's object mode refuses -- asked of a decoder that opens them",
 "utc": "2026-09-10T22:25:10.394280+00:00",
 "commit": "76aa200b06711c2c8c3558ab07a278d901051d17",
 "why": "the report has said since the first round that the titles Dolby refuses are the ones whose object output has never been confirmed. That was true when they were three and there was no third decoder. It is not true now",
 "method": "the same twenty-second cuts the sweep took, decoded twice -- `oadec decode -p 3 --format damf --no-bed-conform` and `truehdd decode --presentation 3` -- and the two `.atmos.audio` files compared by hash. TrueHD is lossless and presentation 3 carries the objects as coded channels, so two correct decoders must agree exactly",
