 },
 "reading": "every one of the 89 streams Dolby's object mode refuses decodes here to object audio byte-identical to an independent decoder's, and so do the fourteen it opens that were taken as a control. The refusal says nothing about whether this decoder is right about those streams. It is the last claim in this report that treated the refused set as unconfirmed, and it is withdrawn",
 "what_it_does_not_say": "that Dolby is wrong. Two non-Dolby decoders agreeing is weaker than either agreeing with Dolby, and the reason that mode refuses them is still unknown",
